+# [human-eye] JARVIS onboarding wizard — Step 3 use-case cards keyboard-unreachable (WCAG 2.1.1 / 4.1.2) + dialog a11y nits
+
+**Date**: 2026-10-30, Cycles 55–56 (~05:00–06:15Z)
+**Surface**: `https://supremeai-studio.pages.dev/chat` (canonical; identical build on `supremeai-studio.vercel.app`)
+**Bundle**: Pages `index-CJP2tBKK.js` / Vercel `index-qPQ9PTs6.js` (static for 11 consecutive cycles; finding pinned to this bundle)
+**Viewport/method**: desktop 1280, keyboard-only walkthrough (Tab/Enter/Escape) cross-checked against mouse path; a11y-tree snapshot as ground truth
+**Context**: wizard = first-run mandatory intercept for every new /chat visitor ("JARVIS Neural Setup", Steps 1–3, z-50 backdrop-blur overlay with "Dismiss for now" escape). Step 1 keyboard sweep already FULL PASS (Cycle 55: Tab order, focus rings, Enter activation).
+
+## Filing core — Step 3 use-case cards are keyboard-unreachable
+
+**Before (keyboard path)** — Tab walk from "Dismiss for now" at Step 3 of 3:
+
+```
+stop1: BUTTON[Back]
+stop2: BUTTON[Finish & Activate]
+stop3: BODY  ← focus escapes the overlay entirely
+stop4+: background page links (SupremeAI home / Chat / About / Sign in …)
+```
+
+The four primary-choice controls receive **zero Tab stops**:
+
+```
+div "Coding & Autonomous Agents"   role=null  tabindex=null  aria-label=null  onclick=present
+div "Deep Research & Learning"     role=null  tabindex=null  aria-label=null  onclick=present
+div "Business, Content & Ops"      role=null  tabindex=null  aria-label=null  onclick=present
+div "Daily Intelligent Assistant"  role=null  tabindex=null  aria-label=null  onclick=present
+```
+
+**After (mouse path, same cards)** — click works and carries a full visual selected state:
+
+```
+clicked card:   border-cyan-400  bg-cyan-500/15          (same cyan token family as Step 1 chooser)
+other cards:    border-white/10  bg-white/[0.02]  hover:bg-white/[0.05]
+```
+
+**Result**: the component already renders selection state and reacts to `onclick`; only the keyboard/AT contract is missing. Keyboard-only and screen-reader users cannot select a use case; screen readers announce the cards as bare `generic` with no role and no activation semantics.
+
+**WCAG**: 2.1.1 Keyboard (Level A) — functionality not operable through keyboard; 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value — control role/state not exposed.
+
+**Impact**: moderate. The wizard is not hard-blocked ("Finish & Activate" is reachable and Enter-activatable without any card selection; "Dismiss for now" works), so this is functional exclusion of an optional-but-prominent choice, not a journey dead-end. Every first-run user passes through this screen.
+
+**Smallest safe fix (no redesign, token-clean)**: render the card container as `<button type="button">` instead of a clickable `div` — inherits focusability, Enter/Space activation, and `button` role for free, keeps all existing classes (`p-3 rounded-xl border cursor-pointer transition …`). While touching the same element: add `aria-pressed={selected}` (the cyan state already exists visually; one attribute exposes it). Zero visual change; the `cursor-pointer` and border classes carry over unchanged.
+
+**Regression test**: (1) Tab walk at Step 3 from "Dismiss for now" must produce 4 card stops between Dismiss and Back; (2) Enter on a card applies the `border-cyan-400` selected class and `aria-pressed=true` while siblings report `false`; (3) a keyboard-only run can complete Step 1 → 2 → 3 → Finish & Activate with a card selection made entirely via Enter.
+
+## Companion nits (same wizard, same fix batch — recorded, severity noted)
+
+| # | Finding | Evidence | Severity |
+|---|---------|----------|----------|
+| N1 | Modal overlay has no focus trap — Tab escapes to the background page while the wizard is open (stop3 = BODY, then background nav links) | Tab walks at Step 2 (8 stops) and Step 3 (7 stops) | Moderate nit; APG modal-dialog pattern expects trap + return focus |
+| N2 | Escape does not close the wizard (pressed twice with overlay open, a11y tree unchanged); only the visible "Dismiss for now" button dismisses | Escape re-test at Step 1, immediate re-snapshot | Nit (visible escape hatch exists; APG: Escape SHOULD close) |
+| N3 | Step 2 preset name chips (JARVIS/FRIDAY/SHADHIN/NEXUS) are quick-fill semantics — Enter fills the textbox (verified: input value syncs to "FRIDAY") but chips carry no `aria-pressed`/selected state; classNames byte-identical across chips | computed style + className diff probes | Nit; if chips are intended as a chooser rather than quick-fill, they need the same `aria-pressed` treatment as the fix above |
+| N4 | Step 1 salutation chooser carries no `aria-checked`/`aria-pressed` (selection lives in `border-cyan-400` class only) — carried over from Cycle 55 own-log | C55 record | Nit (below filing threshold alone) |
+
+**Positive results worth keeping** (all keyboard-verified): Step 1/2/3 Tab order is logical = visual; focus ring 2px `rgb(0,243,255)` on every stop; Step 2 Back returns to Step 1 with full state retention (chosen name "FRIDAY" propagated into the Step 1 heading and the textbox); "Finish & Activate" and "Dismiss for now" are aria-labeled and Enter-activatable; the incidental satisfaction-survey overlay that appeared mid-walkthrough ("Dismiss survey" + 1–5 scale) is keyboard-operable and keyboard-dismissible.
+
+## Why file now
+
+1. Every first-run visitor hits this wizard; keyboard exclusion on its primary choice screen is a Level A failure, above the established aria-nit threshold.
+2. The expected near-term rebuild (env-injection fix for the degraded viewer mode, #2736 lineage) is the natural vehicle — a11y attributes are one-liners in that same pass; filing now pins bundle-stable evidence before any rebuild reshuffles the surface.
+3. Dedup clean (below) and the bridge channel currently has no open wizard/a11y item.
+
+## Alternatives rejected
+
+- **Four separate issues (one per nit)** — the intake probe auto-closes issues once the report PR merges (structural pattern confirmed in Cycles 48/53 on #2736/#2912); micro-issues would multiply that churn for zero tracking gain. One consolidated WO instead.
+- **Defer to a healthy build** — bundle is static across 11 cycles and the wizard is identical on both CD targets; the degraded viewer mode does not affect wizard DOM (verified: the overlay renders and behaves identically while the config degradation persists in console). Waiting only risks losing the pinned evidence.
+- **Treat as label-only nit** — keyboard exclusion of the primary choice control is functional (2.1.1), not cosmetic; the nit column is reserved for N1–N4 which genuinely are below-threshold individually.
+
